# short-description: Create SD card image with a boot partition
#
# Every byte of this image is pushed over USB on each flash (DFU: ~6 MB/s,
# fastboot: skips empty blocks but still writes what is there), so the
# partitions are sized to their content, not to the eMMC. Only the last
# partition (userfs) is grown to fill the device at first boot by
# resize-helper.service; boot and root stay the size they are here.
#
# boot: tiboot3.bin, tispl.bin, u-boot.img and uEnv.txt, ~2.5 MB. Only the
# SD-card boot path reads it (eMMC boots from boot0); 16 MB is plenty.
#
# root: bitbake's ROOTFS_SIZE already carries the slack for the rootfs
# (IMAGE_OVERHEAD_FACTOR and IMAGE_ROOTFS_EXTRA_SPACE in
# vtlinux-image-kiosk.inc). Without --overhead-factor 1.0 wic multiplies
# that padded size by its own 1.3 default again: 304 MB of content became a
# 470 MB partition with 175 MB free.
part --source bootimg-partition --fstype=vfat --label boot --active --align 1024 --use-uuid --fixed-size 16M
part / --source rootfs --fstype=ext4 --label root --align 1024 --use-uuid --overhead-factor 1.0
part --source rawcopy --sourceparams="file=vtlinux-image-userfs-vtlinux-${MACHINE}.userfs.ext4" --ondisk mmcblk0 --fstype=ext4 --label userfs

bootloader --ptable gpt